abstract: "A small business chart of accounts is the numbered list of every account the books post to, grouped by type: assets, liabilities, equity, income, cost of sales and operating expenses. Each industry then adds a few lines of its own, such as a trust account and the matching client liability for a law firm. The CSVs here give that layout for five industries."
keywords:
